# Repair plan for /go-test/go-test:fixture.buildcodefix.tests.suite::TestAddSumsItsArguments

## Diagnosis

One failing test, one planted production defect, entirely inside the
declared write root.

`services/calc/calc.go` declares `func Add(a, b int) int` whose doc
comment states it "returns the sum of a and b", but the body computes
`return a - b`. The subtraction is the defect — the comment immediately
below it even admits it was planted deliberately.

`tests/suite/add_test.go` calls `calc.Add(2, 3)` and requires `5`. With
subtraction it gets `2 - 3 = -1`, producing exactly the observed
failure:

```
add_test.go:19: Add(2, 3) = -1, want 5
```

Per `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` and `CLAUDE.md`, the test is
the specification and `services/calc` is the only writable tree. Nothing
outside that tree needs to change: the module path
(`fixture/buildcodefix`), the package name (`calc`), the exported
symbol name and its signature are all already what the test imports and
calls. Only the arithmetic is wrong.

